  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mishrilal vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of ... on 12 November, 2024 Author: Alok Mathur Bench: Alok Mathur High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:74577 Court No. - 6 Case :- Writ - A No. - 10415 of 2024 Petitioner :- Mishrilal Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of Food Safety And Drug Admi. Lko A Counsel for Petitioner :- Ganesh Kumar Gupta,Rajesh Pratap Singh",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "It is only after the order of transfer has been complied with as the petitioner has joined at the transferred place of posting, he has submitted an application on 09.10.2024 stating that the impugned order of transfer Mishrilal vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of ... on 12 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/192090511/ 1 has been passed in violation of the guidelines issued by the State Government for the transfer session 2024-2025 and also raised certain personal grievances with regard to his family members while assailing the said order. 4. It is in the aforesaid circumstances, the petitioner in the present case, has prayed for quashing of the order of transfer dated 30.06.2024 and for directing the respondents to transfer the petitioner from Agra to Ayodhya or near any district adjacent to Ayodhya. 5. He has submitted that petitioner was transferred by means of order dated 30.06.2024 and he has already complied with the order of transfer dated 30.06.2024. He has further submitted that once the order of transfer has been complied with without any demur and he has estopped from assailing the validity of the said order as the petitioner joined on the transferred is no longer available to assail. 6. He further submits that the action of the petitioner itself indicates that he has accepted the order of transfer dated 30.06.2024 and he cannot be allowed to approbate and reprobate and permitted to challenge the order after his joining ."
  },
